hat do you make of these um  vaccine mandates that we're seeing now  being introduced in the united states we  know lots of companies are requiring  people to be vaccinated and new york  city has become the first  major  urban area that's going to require  people to prove that they've been  vaccinated if they want to go  inside restaurants and bars or gyms  what do you make of that could it  backfire  i mean yes i mean all i mean here in new  york as you said and even here at mount  sinai where i work for our students we  also mandate them to be vaccinated um no  i i think it is a very um good idea i  think it does make a lot of sense i  think like in restaurants in bars and  clubs and venues it protects the people  who work there it also protects the  other audience members and also it  it kind of protects their um extended  network  it protects everyone you know like when  those people go home they might have  small kids at home who might not be able  to get vaccinated yet so it protects the  whole community so um i i think it's a  very good idea and do you think  that the the public information campaign  about these breakthrough infections is  is it helping  or hurting the vaccination drives  well i think it is important that the um  information is um  bought over the right way i mean yes  they are break  infections but the people they get  infected but there's a difference of  being infected and be severely sick and  being admitted to the icu at our  hospital the patient that we see or  admitted to the icu um they're all  people who got not vaccinated and yes we  do test people positive who are  vaccinated but they are not severely  sick so i think that is really um that's  a really important message and this  delta variant that we're dealing with  right now particularly in the united  states  what does it mean for this goal of of 80  or 90 in reaching hurt immunity does it  just shatter that equation  um i don't think in my opinion like the  ideal of hurt immunity uh was never that  um  achievable i mean  as you showed forward i mean in the i  mean here in  in the developed countries about hundred  uh there are about 100 doses per 100  people giving right now i think right  now we have a  70 percent i come out of the ones who  are unelectable but in other parts of  the world they have given 1.5 doses per  100 population and as long as the  majority of the world is poorly  populated there there will be nothing  even close to hurt on immunity and this  will  and i i think for years there will be no  hood immunities though so in the end  for for the next months or even years  people who are not vaccinated eventually  they will become infected  dr neil is heading from mount sinai  global health center tonight dr henry we  appreciate your time and your  insights thank you  thank you
 

